{"id":"4b4f17c2-8f9e-473e-bd6c-37809a624023","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"9ae44f2baf4ff829","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/snapshot.ts","baseline":{"blob":"6e7e04007de75cce23a0d746f8f4607ac2b3c215","start":1575,"end":1718},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","MANAGED_CONFIGS","=","new","Set","(","[","\"","tsconfig.json","\"",",","\"","jsconfig.json","\"",",","\"","eslint.config.js","\"",",","\"","eslint.config.mjs","\"",",","\"","eslint.config.cjs","\"",",","\"",".gitignore","\"","]",")"]},"context":{"before":"b8a5a1426c83aa16","after":"e5f9688534e9790d"}},"payload":{"text":"Root-level config files the EDITOR manages rather than the user: seeded read-only, so workspace-fs enforces it\n(the editor shows the lock + blocks Save, the vscode API and the terminal get a permission error). Matched\nagainst the workspace-relative path, so only the ROOT one is managed — a nested config the user makes stays\ntheirs. (Editor settings aren't seeded as a file: see `editor:settings-defaults` below.)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:26.233Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:26.233Z"}
{"id":"61ce9e3b-ea14-4f28-a004-9e9ad65a7221","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7cbb1744640eb4de","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/snapshot.ts","baseline":{"blob":"6aaa3596d7765c945fdf0df7d7c3aa6073d0add8","start":2240,"end":2345},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","packageDir","(",")",":","string","{","return","path",".","dirname","(","path",".","dirname","(","url",".","fileURLToPath","(","import",".","meta",".","url",")",")",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"e5f9688534e9790d","after":"f1ad7837aa34526a"}},"payload":{"text":"The package's directory (this file is in its build/).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:23.898Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:23.898Z"}
{"id":"6ebf78d4-1db0-4dd9-8c70-990916babda0","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"336d05c5806fbc4c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/snapshot.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0f5bb86289ca1dc0bf25746a7578cd46ee2e57c8","start":5029,"end":5089},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","SETTINGS_DEFAULTS_VIRTUAL","=","\"","editor:settings-defaults","\""]},"context":{"before":"1bbab37695399327","after":"01c3a80f924a4565"}},"payload":{"text":"── Settings defaults (`editor:settings-defaults`) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nThe editor's curated settings (settings-defaults.jsonc — the user's lib/.vscode/settings.json), parsed (JSONC —\ncomments, trailing commas) into the object the workbench registers as CONFIGURATION DEFAULTS, the lowest settings\nlayer. VS Code merges settings layers per key, so a workspace `.vscode/settings.json` that sets only a theme — or\na loaded repo's own — still inherits the eslint fix-all / format-on-save setup for every key it doesn't set, while\nany key it does set wins. That's why no `.vscode/` is seeded into the workspace: it belongs to the user or repo.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:20.225Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:20.225Z"}
{"id":"b0c1dd14-f351-4d50-8d87-184277c5c284","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"69b0551ad18b00fc","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/snapshot.ts","baseline":{"blob":"83e7b434e182bc21abedcc4fe7891c45c51ae799","start":2533,"end":2733},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","nodeModulesRoot","(",")",":","string","|","undefined","{","const","nodeModules","=","utilFs",".","closest","(","packageDir","(",")",",","\"","node_modules","\"",")",";","return","nodeModules","===","undefined","?","undefined",":","path",".","dirname","(","nodeModules",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"f1ad7837aa34526a","after":"34248ee6a74f4359"}},"payload":{"text":"Nearest ancestor directory that has a node_modules (editor's workspace root, for type seeding).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:21.485Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:21.485Z"}
{"id":"e945b94d-bd36-463b-a9cc-e86ff328816f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b8a5a1426c83aa16","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/snapshot.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9a5f8a0dabbae9493a094a09223046888bfbd002","start":1310,"end":1423},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","TEXT","=","new","Set","(","[","\"","ts","\"",",","\"","tsx","\"",",","\"","mjs","\"",",","\"","cjs","\"",",","\"","js","\"",",","\"","jsx","\"",",","\"","json","\"",",","\"","md","\"",",","\"","yml","\"",",","\"","yaml","\"",",","\"","html","\"",",","\"","css","\"",",","\"","txt","\"","]",")"]},"context":{"before":"7ea4161086d5e50c","after":"9ae44f2baf4ff829"}},"payload":{"text":"Text/source extensions worth showing. Anything else (images, tarballs) is dropped; dotfiles\nare kept regardless since they carry no extension.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:27.402Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:27.402Z"}
{"id":"eb06510f-e9ad-4162-bae4-065ea3d10971","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6e6a075e13306db4","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/snapshot.ts","baseline":{"blob":"53d03416116aceac06f9ad16cac3163eb80fea36","start":0,"end":34},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Plugin","}","from","\"","vite","\""]},"context":{"after":"bca5244780e81d0e"}},"payload":{"text":"Bakes a snapshot of the bundled demo workspace into the build as the virtual module\n`editor:workspace`, so the hosted workbench (GitHub Pages) opens on a real sample project — not a\nfixture, not blank. main.tsx imports it and hands it to `createVscodeWindow({ files })`.\n\nSource = the fixed `demo/` directory in this package (NOT git — editor opens on a curated sample,\nnot on its own source). A later File System Access overlay adds a \"real on-disk folder\" source mode\nalongside this one.\n\nA browse snapshot (this file) plus a dependency type surface (editorTypesPlugin, package-types.ts) so the\nin-browser TS language service resolves the demo's imports and reports no phantom errors. And the editor's settings\ndefaults (`editor:settings-defaults`, below), the starter's settings without a `.vscode/` in it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:28.613Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:28.613Z"}
{"id":"00e6dfc0-c96d-44df-9598-591a795c7ee5","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3b186e960d650ef8","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/snapshot.ts","baseline":{"blob":"dfca044026519a1867e23932d3276f35b1be77e8","start":2194,"end":2203},"shape":{"type":"Return","atoms":["return","[","]"]},"context":{"before":"735f62a64a77a2ee","after":"d48a1987cca0a3dc"}},"payload":{"text":"no demo yet → the workbench opens on an empty folder","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T19:04:04.062Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T19:04:04.062Z"}
{"id":"90111b01-cba9-42fd-a3ed-9089484546b8","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"43fd51d753327e82","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/snapshot.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b58828e8d9b44dd85a1d70b1958a96d1a0442b08","start":277,"end":311},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","const","FOLDER","=","\"","/workspace","\""]},"context":{"before":"f1fcb7ec61600937","after":"7ea4161086d5e50c"}},"payload":{"text":"the explorer root the demo files mount under","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T19:04:06.558Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T19:04:06.558Z"}
